<div class="exercise"><div class="ex-q"><p>Why is the hysteresis feedback connected to the non-inverting input?</p>
</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class="ex-s"><p>Positive feedback reinforces a change: once the output starts to switch, the threshold moves to make the switch more certain. Feedback to the inverting input would be negative feedback, which makes a linear amplifier instead.</p>
</div></details></div>
